    "text": "---\nname: space-demo-and-replicate\ndescription: Turn a member's Muse Space into a listed, sellable showcase Space: audit it, produce a 60–90s demo video of one real input becoming one real result, fill its Whop Army Space listing (grouped under the owner), and attach a verified replication kit. Owner approves before anything goes public.\n---\n\n# Space Demo and Replicate — the member listing skill\n\nRun this in the **member's own Muse**, on the member's own keys. It takes one finished Space and produces three things: a demo video, a Whop Army Space listing (unpublished until the owner taps), and a replication kit a buyer's Muse can rebuild from. It composes the existing `replicate_space` skill — do not re-implement the kit rules; load that skill for steps 4–5.\n\n## Autonomous operation — human in the loop, never human as the labor (Dave, 2026-11-24)\n\nThis skill runs **autonomously end to end**. The human's job is judgment at gates, not work between them:\n\n- **Muse does every mechanical step itself**: audit, demo production, packaging, secret scan, bridge submission, polling the verification battery, and — on a NEEDS_WORK result — **fixing the named failures and resubmitting on its own**, up to 3 attempts per failure class. A failure the skill can fix (missing file, bad manifest shape, placeholder left in the prompt) is never handed back to the human as homework.\n- **The human is tapped only at judgment gates**: (1) the price, (2) the demo video approval, (3) the publish flip, (4) anything that would publish, send, or spend beyond this listing. Each gate is one tap with the finished artifact shown inline — never a question the human has to research.\n- **Escalate, don't stall**: after 3 failed attempts at the same check, or any failure whose fix needs a human decision (a real secret found in the kit, a Space whose core flow needs typing), stop and report the exact check, the evidence, and the one decision needed. Silence is not a state — the owner always gets either a gate tap or an escalation, never a dead end.\n- **Massive utility is the bar**: the same autonomous loop serves every Space and agent the owner ever lists — package once, and re-listings, price changes, kit updates, and new Spaces all ride the identical submit → battery → fix → gate path. If a step only works for this one Space, generalize it before moving on.\n\n## Ground rules\n\n- **One input, one result.** The demo shows the Space's single best flow: the one input a user gives (a URL, a name + city, a photo) and the real result it produces. If the Space needs typing or form-filling on camera, that is a defect to report to the owner, not a demo to polish over.\n- **Nothing fabricated.** The demo runs the real Space on a real (or clearly labeled sample) input and shows the real output. No mock results, no sped-up \"processing\" theater, no invented numbers.\n- **Nothing publishes without the owner's tap.** The listing is created `public=false`. The demo video, the price, and the public flip are three separate owner approvals.\n- **No key values anywhere.** Kits list which keys a buyer needs and where they get their own. Values only ever move through secure entry into the buyer's own storage.\n\n## Step 1 — Audit the Space\n\nFollow the audit in `replicate_space`: inspect the Space's surfaces, actions, data model, scheduled refreshes and executor crons (a Space whose queue has no executor is dead — fix or flag before listing). Classify stored data as structure / seed / private; only structure and public seed may travel. Record: the one-input flow, the skills the Space uses, the connectors/keys it needs.\n\n## Step 2 — Produce the demo video\n\n1. Script 60–90 seconds: hook (the result, first 3 seconds) → the one input → the real run → the result up close → one line on how to get it (replicate or buy). No feature tour.\n2. Capture the real Space running (screen capture of the actual flow; the house screen-record lane where available).\n3. Produce through Clip Desk / the video engine backend. Voice in the owner's brand voice where one is saved.\n4. **QA by watching**: full watch-through — frames, audio present for the whole duration, the result on screen is the real output of the run you captured. A failed watch is a redo, not a note.\n5. Host the finished MP4 on the owner's own infra path (the site's public folder pattern). Anonymous file hosts are not a delivery route for listings.\n\n## Step 3 — Fill the listing\n\nCreate or update the Space's Application row (Whop Army bridge, owner session) with:\n- `name`, one-line `description` (the outcome, not the tech), `category`\n- `videoUrl` = the hosted demo from Step 2; `demoKind = \"video\"` (use `\"live\"` + `liveUrl` only when a public live demo truly exists)\n- `screenshotUrl` = a real frame from the demo\n- `priceCents` = the price the **owner** states (0 = free); never invent a price\n- `replicationManifest` = `{ skills: [...], keys: [...], crons: [...] }` from the Step 1 audit\n- `public` stays **false**\n- `handoutOptIn` — the seller sets this **by sentence at submit/resubmit** (\"opt my Space into Handout days\" / \"keep it out\"), never via a web form. Opting in means: on the Space's Free Space of the Day, the seller's agent does 24h Handout visits — visitors' agents may use the Space until midnight ET that day. **The kit is never given** on a Handout; the listing price and the kit stay exactly as set. Omitting the field on a resubmit preserves the existing value.\n\nThe listing renders on /spaces grouped under the owner (their storefront section, their agents and Spaces together) and on the building agent's profile as \"Spaces built by this agent.\"\n\n## Step 4 — Build the replication kit\n\nPer `replicate_space`: README, paste-ready BUILD-PROMPT for the buyer's Muse, core skill folders (SKILL.md + skill.yaml), KEYS checklist (service, purpose, required/optional, where to get it, verification call), data schema, executor + cron definitions. Verify: every named skill exists, every key matches a connector doc, every lane names a live verification. Anything unverified is labeled Unverified in the README.\n\n## Step 5 — Wire and verify the Replicate panel\n\nConfirm the listing's Replicate panel shows the manifest's skills + KEYS checklist with Copy Build Prompt and Download Kit (per `~/workspace/space-replication/REPLICATE-BUTTON-SPEC.md`). Download the kit once yourself and check the zip's contents against the manifest — a kit that lists files it doesn't contain is a failed listing.\n\n## Step 6 — Owner approval and report\n\nShow the owner, in their Muse: the demo video inline, the listing exactly as it will render (name, one-liner, price, category), and the kit contents list. On their tap: flip `public=true` and read the live /spaces page back to prove the listing is up, grouped under them, video playing. Report: listing URL, video URL, kit path, price as listed, and anything left Unverified.\n"
